2026-08-16T13:25:03Z    [HD:Net sales] GATE critic: You anchored FY2026Q2 off “FY2025Q2: net sales $45.3 billion,” but that $45.3b figure appears to be Q2 of fiscal 2024, not fiscal 2025. Home Depot’s Q2 FY2025 (the 13 weeks ending in mid‑summer 2025) reported a different sales number. Using a misdated prior‑year base invalidates the YoY step-up you applied and makes 47,502.1 USDm wrong on period basis.
2026-08-16T13:25:20Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: Wrong fiscal period anchor: you compounded from FY2024Q3 GAAP diluted EPS of $6.29 to estimate FY2026Q3, claiming no prior-year figure existed. The correct like-for-like prior-year comparable for FY2026Q3 is FY2025Q3, which Deere would have reported; using FY2024Q3 skips a year and yields a two-year CAGR instead of a proper prior-year comparison. This period error makes the $6.75971 figure unsupported.
2026-08-16T13:25:22Z    [ADI:Revenue] GATE critic: You cite ADI guidance as “FY2026Q3: forecasting revenue of $3.9 billion, +/- $100 million,” which implies a midpoint of exactly 3,900 USDm. Yet your guidance input is 3,929.25 USDm (“guidance_anchor+signal 3929.25”), and your final estimate is 3,903.94 USDm. There’s no source supporting a $3,929m anchor; using anything other than the documented $3.9b midpoint (3,900 USDm) biases the result and puts it on the wrong basis relative to the stated guidance.
