2026-08-16T13:25:37Z    [ADI:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: The estimate (3.47437 USD/share) for ADI’s FY2026Q3 adjusted diluted EPS exceeds the company’s own guidance range of $3.15–$3.45 (midpoint $3.30 ± $0.15) for that quarter; it is $0.02437 above the guided upper bound $3.45.
2026-08-16T13:25:54Z    [HD:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: Your blended YoY growth is mis-scaled: the stated weights 0.62 and 0.37 for the FY2024Q2→FY2025Q2 and FY2023Q2→FY2024Q2 changes do not sum to 1.0 (0.62+0.37=0.99). With correct normalization, the second weight should be 0.38, yielding a growth of 0.048% (0.2%*0.62 − 0.2%*0.38), not the 0.05% you applied. That means the 4.68251 figure is not consistent with your own methodology and reflects a scaling error in the growth blend.
2026-08-16T13:26:00Z    [ADI:Adjusted gross margin] GATE critic: The “last 4 reported levels” average (71.95%) is built from 69.9, 71.6, 74.1, and 72.2, but in your own source lines those are current vs prior-year pairs: 71.6% (current) vs 69.9% (prior-year) and 72.2% (current) vs 74.1% (prior-year). You incorrectly included the prior-year comparatives (69.9% and 74.1%) as if they were current reported quarters, so the baseline is not an average of four current periods and is on the wrong period/basis. Consequently, the 71.9333% derived from it is invalid.
